      {
        "id": 135497,
        "name": "Donner",
        "username": "Donner",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/{size}/1903_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-05T14:36:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Come ON! Clearly, the best flavor text in the game is on Imbued Vitality.Not just for its immediate silliness, but for everything it implies about the Wraith's character.</p>\n<div><b>Rabk wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;EdgeDS wrote:<br><blockquote>I like Sky-Scraper a lot more than I had thought I would, solely for her flavour text. &nbsp;(Also, she's a lot of fun to play, but really - the flavour text for the whole deck is just SO GOOD!)&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n&nbsp;I second this opinion. I've annoyed our playtest group to death by insisting on reading her flavor text (in character) every time I play one of her cards.\n</blockquote></div>\nDo you also (as my fiancee and I do) clap your hands dramatically when you use the Huge power?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I do!</p>",
